// 003.13, 004.11, 011.14 (T06): an unassigned `Evidenced` fact starts `Unresolved`,
// never halts evaluation with `CHR100`, propagates 3-valued `undetermined` to a guarded
// `Power` (`?undetermined`), and supports explicit fallback rules over `Unresolved(...)`.
// Also verifies all new G3.2 contextual words remain usable as unquoted eFLINT atoms (`D17`).
Fact legacy-atom-compat Identified by Evidenced, Finding, Established, Refuted, Unresolved, Conflicted, SubmitEvidence, RetractEvidence, Note, Confidential, Standard, Resolves.
Fact officer Identified by Off1.
Fact applicant Identified by App1.
Evidenced Fact related-party Identified by applicant.
Fact review-required Identified by applicant
  Holds when Unresolved(related-party(applicant)).
Fact loan-approved Identified by applicant.

Power approve-loan Actor officer Related to applicant
  Holds when !related-party(applicant)
  Valid when !related-party(applicant)
  Creates loan-approved(applicant).

Scenario unresolved-related-party {
  ?Unresolved(related-party(App1)).
  ?review-required(App1).
  ?undetermined approve-loan(Off1, App1).
  ?!valid approve-loan(Off1, App1).
  approve-loan(Off1, App1).
  ?!loan-approved(App1).
  SubmitEvidence !related-party(App1) By "registry-cert".
  ?Refuted(related-party(App1)).
  ?!review-required(App1).
  ?!undetermined approve-loan(Off1, App1).
  ?valid approve-loan(Off1, App1).
  approve-loan(Off1, App1).
  ?loan-approved(App1).
}
